<section id="faq" class="section alt">
  <div class="wrap narrow">
    <h2>FAQ</h2>
    <details><summary>How many math questions are on the GMAT?</summary><p>The Quantitative Reasoning section has 21 Problem Solving questions in 45 minutes. Data Insights (20 questions) also uses math skills — especially Data Sufficiency and table/graph questions.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Is the free session really free?</summary><p>Yes. It's a 30-minute 1-on-1 Zoom call with no payment details and no obligation to join the bootcamp.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Can I use a calculator?</summary><p>Not on Quant. An on-screen calculator is available only in Data Insights, so we train fast mental-math and estimation techniques.</p></details>
    <details><summary>What if I miss a live class?</summary><p>Recordings and practice sets are posted to your secure student dashboard.</p></details>
    <details><summary>When should I start?</summary><p>Ideally 6–10 weeks before your test date so you finish the bootcamp with time left for full practice tests.</p></details>
  </div>
</section>

